From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:08:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Name no rpmalloc mapping on iOS: the name hook allocates

Every mapping rpmalloc makes names itself through rp_name_hook, which on
iOS is FEX's VirtualName, and VirtualName logs each name (the first 256)
through LogMan, which allocates. So a mapping made for an allocation
allocated again before rpmalloc had recorded the mapping. On a thread with
no heap yet the nested allocation made another heap; on a heap with no
partial span for the size class it mapped another span; and so on until
the log's cap of 256 names stopped the recursion. On 2026-09-28 Hollow
Knight's second thread, as it started, made 231 heaps that way, and 232
small spans for 64-byte blocks: each level set its own span as the heap's
partial one, so each span kept the one 64KB page it gave out and lost the
other 255. That was 3.7GB of the 16GB FEX host band, a quarter of it,
before the first frame. On iOS a name is a no-op apart from that log, so
os_set_page_name now names nothing there.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-fex-band.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c b/rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c
index c6da961..2034703 100644
--- a/rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c
+++ b/rpmalloc/rpmalloc.c
@@ -853,6 +853,22 @@ get_page_aligned_size(size_t size) {
 
 static void
 os_set_page_name(void* address, size_t size) {
+#if defined(_WIN32) && defined(FEX_IOS_HOST)
+	/* Playport: no names for rpmalloc's own mappings on iOS. The name hook is
+	 * FEX's VirtualName, which logs each name (the first 256), and the log
+	 * allocates. A mapping made for an allocation therefore allocated again
+	 * before the mapping was recorded: on a thread with no heap yet the nested
+	 * allocation made another heap, and on a heap with no partial span it
+	 * mapped another span, and so on until the log's cap stopped it. On
+	 * 2026-09-28 Hollow Knight's second thread went 231 levels deep twice
+	 * over: 231 heaps, and 232 small spans of which each kept one 64KB page in
+	 * use and lost the rest, because every level set its own span as the
+	 * heap's partial one. That was 3.7GB of the 16GB FEX host band, a quarter
+	 * of it, before the first frame. A name has no other use on iOS. */
+	(void)address;
+	(void)size;
+	return;
+#endif
   const char* name = os_huge_pages ? global_config.huge_page_name : global_config.page_name;
 #if defined(__linux__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 	if ((address == MAP_FAILED) || !name) {
